# Build context excludes for `docker buildx build -f Dockerfile.ce` — buildx
# picks up a `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore` automatically when it exists, ahead
# of the plain `.dockerignore` used for the main image. This is a copy of
# that file plus every commercial path, so `ee/` never enters the build
# context at all (not merely "excluded from the final image") — see
# Dockerfile.ce's header comment and docs/architecture/commercial-layer.md.
#
# The excluded paths below must be kept in step with `COMMERCIAL_PATHS` in
# scripts/foss.mjs, the single source of truth for the license carve-out
# (scripts/__tests__/foss.test.ts asserts *that* list against LICENSE). This
# file can't import from foss.mjs the way the test does — .dockerignore has
# no templating — so it's hand-kept in sync instead. If this list and
# COMMERCIAL_PATHS drift, the no-ee guardrail in
# .github/workflows/release.yml catches it before any image is pushed: it
# fails the job on any `ee` directory found in the built image's filesystem.

node_modules
.next
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
coverage
.nyc_output
.DS_Store
*.log
test
**/__tests__
docs
debates
tickets
plans
deploy
repo-info.md
README.md

# Commercial code — the actual point of this file. Keep in step with
# COMMERCIAL_PATHS in scripts/foss.mjs.
ee
app/api/app/(ee)
app/api/webhooks/(ee)
